<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabriz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tabriz is a city in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, historically one of the principal commercial and political centres of the region. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> it became a major hub of trade where Mongol, Persian, Armenian and European merchants met. In 1501 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a> captured Tabriz and proclaimed himself Shah, making it the first capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>, though it was later repeatedly contested with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tabriz.jpg" alt="Tabriz" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: user:Elmju · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tabriz_Municipality_Sa%27at_Tower.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
